t=Table(data,colWidths=[195,70,70,70,70]);t.setStyle(TableStyle([('FONTNAME',(0,0),(-1,0),'Helvetica-Bold'),('FONTSIZE',(0,0),(-1,-1),9),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),7),('LINEBELOW',(0,0),(-1,-1),.5,HexColor('#b2c3b5'))]));story.append(t);story.append(Spacer(1,15));p(latency_note);p(f'All {audit["trial_rows"]} expected rows are present. Independently replayed detected traces: {audit["independent_replays"]}. False positives on both clean labels:0. Full raw per-seed results and undiscovered targets are included. No statistical superiority is established.');page()
h('4 / Replaying a real generated candidate');p('This example comes from an actual accepted Apertus output. It targets a deliberately injected synthetic fault. Full original candidate, final answer, timing and complete observations are retained in results/demo-counterexample.json and model-candidates.jsonl.');p('Target: '+example['payload']['mutant']);story.append(Preformatted(json.dumps(example['payload']['minimized'],indent=2),styles['Code2']));p('Independent command: python track_2b/src/replay.py bundle.json');p('The bundle includes original and minimized operations, per-step reference/target observations, provenance and SHA256. A fresh Python process validates it without a model. SHA256 detects accidental edits; it is not an authenticated signature.');h('Controls and deployment evidence');p('Six positive canaries each detect a known injected fault; correct behavior is clean. A deliberately disabled oracle fails those canaries. Tampered bundles, forbidden operations, invalid field types, too many keys and excessive sequence lengths are rejected.');p('Docker image builds locally. Root make run starts the service. A network-none Docker run replays recorded evidence and controls. The local adapter rejects non-local hosts. Three runtime socket snapshots show loopback communication only; they are observations, not an exhaustive packet or syscall audit.');p(ui_note);p('Reference equivalence does not establish the real-world billing contract. The synchronous simulation does not test genuine concurrent transport, asynchronous callbacks or real streaming.');page()
h('5 / Reproducibility, limits and sources');p('Code version: '+version);p(f'Tested host: {hardware["cpu"]}, {hardware["memory_gib"]}GiB RAM, {hardware["os"]}; native arm64 runtime and Python{hardware["python"]}. Shared system load was not controlled.');p('From a clean checkout, run make run at repository root. The Docker application listens on localhost19564. Recorded-response inspection/replay works without a model. Live generation needs separately provisioned local Apertus and LLM_NAME, LLM_BASE_URL, LLM_API_KEY settings. See docs/REPRODUCE.md for exact commands and model digest.');p('This prototype tests a narrow, synthetic protocol. Schema acceptance is distinct from path fidelity. Repaired repetitions are not independent heldout results. The reference itself needs independent owner review. No production fault, customer saving, real-provider effect, security audit or Swiss cloud deployment is claimed.');p('Next work: independently review the protocol; add real asynchronous transport; freeze new untouched tasks; compare stronger baseline settings and measure repeated model draws before estimating incremental practical value.');h('Authorship and licensing');p('New code/tasks were created within this project on 15 October 2026. Official template copyright is retained. Code/template: Apache-2.0. Report/documentation: CC-BY-4.0. Authored synthetic task data: CDLA-Permissive-2.0. External model/runtime/dependency licences apply.');p('Codex assisted implementation, protocol, experiment plumbing and local materials. Apertus 1.5 alone produced runtime model candidates and did not grade them. No old competition project was reused.');h('References');
